jobs.description:
Datashift is a very fast growing consultancy team with a focus on delivering solutions that answer business questions with data and facts. For one of our fastest growing practices, we are looking for a skilled Consultant with hands-on experience audit and process analysis.

Do you have 2 to 5 years of experience of which at least 2 to 3 years in the field data, cloud technology, (IT) audit and/or process analysis. And the prospect of helping to grow a company that believes in together creating an impact with Data at our customers sounds good? Then we are delighted to receive your personal application and we’ll contact you for an interview and a (virtual) cup of coffee.

Your responsibilities
• Support clients in their journey towards becoming data driven by bridging the gap between business and technology;
• Able to understand the strategic goals of a company, pinpoint the value of data;
• Translate the above in a clear well defined roadmap and understand which approach to use when (pilots & pocs vs roadmap);
• You are responsible for the overall quality of delivery and coaching of your more junior colleagues;
• 
Participate in customer advisory on the set-up of data departments and teams (incl. defining roles and responsibilities).



Your qualifications
• 2 to 5 years of experience in consulting or service-oriented environments of which at least 2 in the area of data or strategic data roadmaps; or in (IT) audit and process analysis;
• Able to deliver high profile activities against tight deadlines;
• Outstanding problem solving skills;
• Knowledge of data landscapes within an organization and understand the end to end dataflows (source to output / consumer);
• Excellent leadership, communication (written and oral) and interpersonal skills;
• Proven success in contributing to a team-oriented environment;
• Master degree in the field of Business Economics, Business Analytics, Information Management or equivalent by experience;
• 
Fluent in Dutch and/or French and English.

To further grow our Modern Data Platform Practice, we are currently looking for a skilled Power BI Expert.

Do you have at least 3 years of experience in designing and building data solutions with Power BI? You want to further develop your abilities & knowledge by working together with highly skilled, helpful and fun colleagues? You are not afraid to be challenged intellectually and personally?

If so, send us your CV and we’ll contact you for an interview and a cup of coffee.


Your responsibilities

• You’re able to work independently on a Power BI assignment;
• Analyze user requirements and design business intelligence solutions;
• Model the data according to business and technical requirements;
• Perform data analysis and generate insights;
• Create visualizations and dashboards;
• Actively participate in knowledge building and sharing;
• Stay up to date with new features and releases in Power BI (and Fabric);
• 
Communicate findings and insights effectively to stakeholders.



Your qualifications

• A minimum of 3 years of experience in speaking with and understanding the needs of clients;
• Between 3 and 5 years of experience with visualization tools such as Power BI and/or Tableau and/or Qlik and/or Looker;
• Experience with DAX, Power Query and SQL
• Hands-on experience with data modeling;
• Knowledge of best practices in Power BI for both data visualization and VertiPaq internals;
• Familiarity with ETL processes and data warehousing concepts;
• Fluent in Dutch and/or French and English;
• Strong communication and interpersonal skills;
• Problem-solving abilities and attention to detail.

Your growth path

• Further grow our Modern Data Platform Practice;
• Continuous learning on projects as well as through training;
• Participate in knowledge building through our competence centers;
• Gradually, you’ll assume more responsibility and grow to a coaching role for more junior colleagues
